course: dictionary
lesson: 887
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one to use. Birch can mean a tree, the wood of that tree, or an old punishment. The clues in the sentence tell you which.
explain: «Birch bark is white and oak bark is rough and cracked.» Bark is the outside covering of a tree, and the sentence compares birch with oak, so birch means the tree here.
explain: «Birch furniture» is different. Furniture is made of wood, so birch means the wood itself. When a sentence is about history and punishment, it means the old meaning: a bundle of birch twigs.
fact: A birch is a tall, thin tree with smooth white or silver bark.
fact: Birch bark peels off in thin layers.
fact: «Birch» can also mean the wood of the tree, as in «birch furniture».
fact: In old times, a birch was a bundle of twigs used to beat people as punishment. This meaning is old-fashioned now.
fact: Birches grow in cool places such as Britain, Ireland, Canada and the northern USA.
exercise: «In winter, bark, buds and shape still tell trees apart: ash has black buds, beech has long pointed buds, birch bark is white and oak bark is rough and cracked.» What colour is birch bark? | Black | Red-brown | *White | Green
exercise: «Birch furniture» uses birch in which sense? | *The wood of the tree | A tall mountain | A small green flower | A bundle of twigs used for punishment
exercise: «In winter, bark, buds and shape still tell trees apart: ash has black buds, beech has long pointed buds, birch bark is white and oak bark is rough and cracked.» Which tree has long pointed buds? | *Beech | Birch | Ash | Oak
test: «Birches have white bark and small triangular leaves, are often the first trees to grow on open land.» What does this tell you about birches? | *They are often the first trees to grow on open land | They only grow in hot deserts | They have black bark | They have round, purple leaves
test: In science lessons, how is the silver birch easy to spot? | *Its white bark | Its loud singing | Its tall, dark shadow | Its red berries
exam: «Grasses and trees like birch and hazel are pollinated by the wind.» How are birch flowers pollinated? | *By the wind | By water | By birds | By bees
